# Dockerfile-specific ignore file for mayhem/Dockerfile (BuildKit convention: a
# file named <dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile takes precedence
# over the context-root .dockerignore for THAT build only).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: upstream ships its own root .dockerignore
# (`* ` / allowlist only `**/*.toml`, `**/*.rs`, `**/*.h`, `**/*.hpp`, `qns`,
# `Cargo.lock`) for ITS OWN Docker tooling. That allowlist would silently strip
# .git, mayhem/, .github/, fuzz/corpus/ seed data, etc. from our build context —
# breaking the "COPY the full repo incl. .git" contract (SPEC — the grader/PATCH
# tier needs real `mayhem`-branch history baked into the image) without ever
# touching (and thus never modifying) upstream's own .dockerignore, keeping this
# integration purely additive.
#
# Goal here: bake in the FULL repo (including .git history), dropping only local
# build artifacts and editor/OS cruft.

# ── Build outputs / local cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/target/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
**/__pycache__/

# ── Editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
